 "title": "County Clerk / Register of Deeds",
 "text": "County Clerk / Register of Deeds\nHome\nGovernment Commissioners\nBoard of Equalization\nDepartments Assessor\nCounty Clerk / Register of Deeds\nTreasurer\nCounty Attorney\nCounty Court\nDistrict Court\nElection\nSheriff\nVeteran's Services\nZoning\nRoad\nExtension Office\nServices Handyman\nPublic Transit\nAgenda\nInformational Links\nBoard Minutes\n​​Morrill County Nebraska\n​​​​Register of Deeds\nMorrill County Marriage License\nCertified Copy\nReal Estate Transfer Form 521 & Affidavit\nBirth Certificate\nRecording Guidelines and Fees\nMarriage License Information\nTo obtain a marriage license, you will both need to come to the County Clerk's office between 7:30 am - 3:30 pm Monday -Thursday and 7:30 am - 11:00 am Fridays. You will need to complete the Marriage License Worksheet, have a valid id and $50.00 cash or check. We do not take credit cards.\nPlease call if you have any questions.\n​\n​\nDeath Certificate\nTobacco License\nProperty Valuation Protest Form 422\nMarriage License Worksheet\nCertificate of Exemption for 5B\nDocumentary Stamp\nInformational Links\nCertificate Of Exemption Deeds To Trustees\nExemption Application Form 451\nProperty Evaluation Protest Instructions\nDocumentary Stamp Tax Exemptions\n​​​ Morrill County Clerk\nRegister of Deeds\nCandace D. Panas\nP.O. Box 610\nBridgeport, NE 69336\nPhone 308-262-0860\nFax: 308-262-2260\nEmail: ​clerk@morrillcountyne.gov\nThe County Clerk's duties include recording all proceedings of the board and attending all its meetings. They also must attend all meetings of the County Board of Equalization. The Clerk must countersign all warrants issued by the board which have been signed by the chairman. Special duties, as required by\n​law may also be necessary. The Clerk must keep a record of all the official bonds and a record of the layout, changes and improvements to all roads. The Clerk must also report to the Secretary of State the names of all county officials, their signatures, and their seals of office before February 1. The County Clerk may also appoint a deputy for whose acts the clerk will be responsible. The County Treasurer, Sheriff, Register of Deeds, or Surveyor may not be appointed as deputies.\nCopyright © Morrill County Nebraska. All Rights Reserved.\nView on Mobile",
